    {
      "id": "reg-m3-tbs2-ex1",
      "title": "Asset and elected deduction",
      "html": "<p>Eligible equipment basis is $160,000. The permitted Section 179 deduction is $40,000. No taxable-income or other limitation changes that amount.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "reg-m3-tbs2-ex2",
      "title": "Supplied training rates",
      "html": "<p>For this exercise, bonus depreciation is 50% of basis remaining after Section 179. Ordinary first-year depreciation is 20% of the remaining basis after bonus. These supplied rates are not a universal statement of current bonus law.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "<h3>Basis after Section 179</h3><p>$160,000 − $40,000 = $120,000.</p><h3>Bonus deduction under the supplied rate</h3><p>50% × $120,000 = $60,000.</p><h3>Ordinary first-year depreciation</h3><p>20% × ($120,000 − $60,000) = $12,000.</p><h3>Adjusted basis after all stated deductions</h3><p>$160,000 − $40,000 − $60,000 − $12,000 = $48,000.</p>"
